                    {
                        "sense_id": "2b2e972d-288a-3c9c-81a9-610b7b17a604",
                        "entry_id": "c75a2cd3-27a2-3387-b62d-d39448a20650",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large 18th-century punchbowl, usually of silver, fluted and scalloped."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dbc478b1-75ee-4f66-92f9-234c99a1008b",
                                "sense_id": "2b2e972d-288a-3c9c-81a9-610b7b17a604",
                                "text": "In the taper-lit, perhaps pre-sixteeth-century room—a piece of Laughing and Triumphing needlework in the style of Rubens completely hid the walls—the capacious oval of the dinner-table, crowned by a monteith bowl filled with slipper-orchids, showed agreeably enough."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "651092ac-0def-472b-a578-7be30f5c3e8f",
                                "sense_id": "2b2e972d-288a-3c9c-81a9-610b7b17a604",
                                "text": "The Punch is a secret Receipt of the Landlord, including but not limited to peach brandy, locally distill’d Whiskey, and milk. A raft of long Icicles broken from the Eaves floats upon the pale contents of the great rustick Monteith."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
